<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Luis Donaldo Colosio</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1950">1950</a>–<a href="/years/1994">1994</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Luis Donaldo Colosio was a Mexican politician and the presidential candidate of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/institutional-revolutionary-party">Institutional Revolutionary Party</a> in 1994. A former party president and minister of social development, he was shot dead at a campaign rally in Tijuana on 23 March 1994. His murder, in a year of rebellion and crisis, deepened distrust of the ruling party, and Ernesto Zedillo replaced him as candidate.</p></div>
